            <ArticleTitle>Endovascular treatment of a coronary artery bypass graft to right ventricle fistula with balloon embolization.</ArticleTitle>
            <Pagination>
                <MedlinePgn>e50-2</MedlinePgn>
            </Pagination>
            <Abstract>
                <AbstractText>Fistula formation between a coronary artery bypass graft and a cardiac cavity is an uncommon finding. We describe a case of transcatheter occlusion of a coronary artery bypass graft to right ventricle fistula in a patient presenting with a subacute inferior myocardial infarction.</AbstractText>
            </Abstract>
